 lastFrame = now;
```
But tool content shows `let lastFrame = performance.now();`? Looking at text: `let lastFrame = performance.now();` yes? Actually I see at bottom: `let lastFrame = performance.now();` and `let dt = (now - lastFrame) / 1000;`? The tool content shows:
```
  let lastFrame = performance.now();

